WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.701
-I have an announcement
to make tonight.

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:04.234
I have --
I wanted to do so--

00:00:04.234 --> 00:00:06.501
Jennifer Lopez and I wanted
to do something together.

00:00:06.501 --> 00:00:07.701
Always.
-Always.

00:00:07.701 --> 00:00:10.167
-Yeah. And I can tell
the audience wants it.

00:00:10.167 --> 00:00:13.501
You know?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.501 --> 00:00:17.367
And so I said to Jennifer,
I go, "Let's do a song."

00:00:17.367 --> 00:00:19.167
And she -- she said, "No."

00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:20.434
Immediately.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.434 --> 00:00:21.767
Just -- not even --
didn't even think about it.

00:00:21.767 --> 00:00:22.834
Didn't even think about it.

00:00:22.834 --> 00:00:24.200
Politely said no.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.300
So I said, "What about maybe --
how about like a rom-com?

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:29.667
Romantic movie.
You know, we could do --

00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:31.567
Didn't even --
She almost hung up the phone.

00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:33.300
So, I said, "All right,
let's think of something."

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.634
We did want to work together.

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:36.767
Maybe it was more me that
wanted to work with Jennifer.

00:00:36.767 --> 00:00:38.701
[ Laughter ]
But I go, let's do something --

00:00:38.701 --> 00:00:41.634
I go, "I've written kids books,
you know, children's books."

00:00:41.634 --> 00:00:43.634
She goes --
And I know she loves her kids.

00:00:43.634 --> 00:00:45.501
They're always here with her
when she's on the show.

00:00:45.501 --> 00:00:47.167
I go, "Let's do --" She goes,
"That'd be a great idea."

00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:49.133
So, I came up with a great idea.

00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:50.834
This is it.

00:00:50.834 --> 00:00:52.968
"Con Pollo."
-Oh!

00:00:52.968 --> 00:00:54.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:57.534
-"Con Pollo"!
So, here is the idea.

00:00:57.534 --> 00:00:59.734
"Con pollo"
means "with chicken."

00:00:59.734 --> 00:01:01.801
When you think of con pollo,
you think of --

00:01:01.801 --> 00:01:03.000
-Arroz con pollo.
-No, no, no.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.167
-Oh, eating a chicken.

00:01:04.167 --> 00:01:05.634
-No, you're not eating
the chicken in this.

00:01:05.634 --> 00:01:07.267
This -- you're friends
with the chicken.

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:09.534
-Your friends eat the chicken.
-No one eats the chicken.

00:01:09.534 --> 00:01:11.701
[ Laughter ]
Chicken is your buddy in this.

00:01:11.701 --> 00:01:13.300
No one eats the chicken
at all in this.

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:15.634
"Con Pollo,"
it's a this-or-that book.

00:01:15.634 --> 00:01:17.801
Okay? And basically, like,
what you do is you --

00:01:17.801 --> 00:01:21.200
you learn Spanish as it --
you teach your kids Spanish.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.000
So you go, "Do you want to go
to the beach,

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.667
or do you want to go
to la playa con pollo?"

00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:27.067
-Oh!

00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:30.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:32.567
-And I dedicate this to my
high school Spanish teachers,

00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:38.033
Mrs. Shermer, Mrs. Wasinski,
and Mrs. Houlihan.

00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:40.801
[ In Irish accent ]
The best Spanish teachers around

00:01:40.801 --> 00:01:42.968
this side --
this side of the rainbow.

00:01:42.968 --> 00:01:46.567
Mrs. Houlihan was there
to teach me my Spanish.

00:01:46.567 --> 00:01:49.434
[ Normal voice ] But I do want
to give a shout-out to them.

00:01:49.434 --> 00:01:51.501
Some are not with us.

00:01:51.501 --> 00:01:55.067
But your names will now be in
schools and libraries forever.

00:01:55.067 --> 00:01:57.234
So, thank you so much.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:57.234 --> 00:01:58.801
"Con Pollo."

